Z||000000||Blade||08-22-2000||03:50 PM||||What are my turbo options? <BR>what kind of cost would i be looking at. On a stock v6. Im interested in info on kits and/or full installs. How hard will it be on the engine? And lastly is this a cheaper easier option to the engine swaps?<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-22-2000||04:09 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com</A>   about $3800 for their turbo kits... the design one kits will need a flange cut and rewelded for clearance for piping for an intercooler if an intercooler is in your future.. yes a turbo is a good upgrade to a good motor but if the motor has any kind of wear (blows smoke all the time or has bad compression) tacking on a turbo will just accelerate it's failure and force you to buy a new motor sooner than you had anticipated... if you have a good fresh motor jump all over a turbo kit! Welcome to the forum!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blade||08-23-2000||11:56 AM||||Cool i checked out the link. Are there any other turbo kit manufacturers and/or people who actually will do the install. Also how will it affect smog tests?<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||08-23-2000||01:25 PM||||since your in Cali. try <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  for their install prices and thier schedule or <A HREF="http://fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://fieroshop.net/</A>  a  fellow Forum members shop... probly another $5-700 for the install...  10 hours at $60 an hour + shop supplies and a case of beer.. about $700...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> thats just my guess... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||08-24-2000||03:06 PM||||I have Turbos on my 2.8 now, but I bought it that way. I am putting a NorthStar in it, for about 2,800. I am going to drive it for a while with just the NorthStar and then try and add the old Turbo to it. Im my opinion, I would go for a V8, and then Turbo it if you still want to.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Blade||08-24-2000||03:37 PM||||well im finding out that in cali smog may be an issue with the turbos. Super charger may be ok but i dont wanna lose the AC. I need to find out if how an engine swap is gonna affect my smog crap. since that looks to be my option. Also gonna look into nos.<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||08-24-2000||03:59 PM||||Seanh,<P>Not to flame you or anything but I don't think your turbo(s) will work on the N*. Your dealing with a motor with a lot more cubic displacement then the 2.8. The turbos need to be matched with the motor. If the turbo is too small it max out too soon and won't do you much good.<P>What type of turbo set are you using? Custom or something like Design One or Miller-Woods? If your setup is in good shape I may e interested in purchasing it from you when you've finished your N* project. Just send me an E-mail if interested.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000007||1FST2M6||08-24-2000||04:52 PM||||Nitrous is nice but it gets pricey after a while.. at $30 to sill a bottle and yeah if you have slf control (i didn't) you can use it only at the track under the perfect conditions and save a few bucks but a turbo kit will ALWAYS be there it doesn't run out.. and you can retain all your smog system with a turbo system... and if you HAVE to have a CARB # i'll send you a CARB badge from a Greddy turbo kit. Nitrous is SOOOOO SWEET! but it runs out... and uum Seanh you said Turbo(s)? running a bi-turbo set up?  intercooled?  what turbos T25 or 03s?   ||||reg||1
